      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Toyonaka’s humid subtropical climate brings warm summers, with August averages near 28.7 °C, and cool winters around 5.1 °C.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyonaka"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2001 Toyonaka earned Special city status, gaining greater local autonomy, and later became a core city in 2012.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyonaka",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The southern part of Toyonaka hosts a concentrated manufacturing district, while the northern highlands overlook the Osaka Plain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
